
  The failure mode I most want to avoid is destroying your tasks. So: [1mcorrupt localStorage is never cleared.[0m The raw
  string is copied to a backup key, the app starts empty, and a banner says so. Quota-exceeded surfaces rather than
  silently dropping writes. localStorage unavailable (private browsing) runs in memory with a banner that nothing will
  persist. Unparseable dates degrade to "no due date" and flag the task rather than throwing.

  [1mTesting[0m

  [38;5;153mrules.js[39m is pure and is the main target — table-driven over [38;5;153m(task, now)[39m → expected items, including boundaries at
  exactly-due and exactly-the-staleness-threshold. Then key-stability tests (changing [38;5;153mdueAt[39m changes the key; an
  unrelated edit doesn't), ledger dismiss/persist/prune, and the store's mutation path.

  [1mExplicitly not in scope[0m

  No rule editor, no snooze, no browser notifications, no tags, no recurring tasks, no sync. Each is an addition on top
  of this, and none of them change these interfaces.

  One thing I need from you before writing the spec — this is a new project with no tooling configured, and setting it
  up now is far cheaper than retrofitting:

